From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:10:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini station: add the PMIC keys

The Esc key is the MT6351 power key, and the station has no PMIC keys
node, so a press reports nothing and can't wake a blanked console. Add
the node and report it as KEY_ESC, as Gemian does.

The bootloader selects boot2 from the PMIC home key, so describe that
too, with Gemian's KEY_SEND. The driver assigns the PMIC keys by child
order, so power must come first.

The driver rewrites the long-press policy at probe, and an absent mode
disables the reset. Set the policy from Gemian's configuration:
one-key reset, eleven seconds.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 .../dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts   | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 78626fc34..e21d6f74c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -291,6 +291,22 @@ &thermal {
 };
 
 &pmic {
+	keys {
+		compatible = "mediatek,mt6351-keys";
+		/* Gemian's policy; an absent mode disables the long-press reset. */
+		mediatek,long-press-mode = <1>;
+		power-off-time-sec = <11>;
+
+		/* The driver assigns the PMIC keys by child order: power, then home. */
+		power-key {
+			linux,keycodes = <KEY_ESC>;
+		};
+
+		home-key {
+			linux,keycodes = <KEY_SEND>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	fuel-gauge {
 		compatible = "mediatek,mt6351-fuel-gauge";
 		io-channels = <&pmic_adc MT6351_AUXADC_BATADC>;
-- 
